    "Runtime restore validates all candidate segments and all reserved nested compiled children before parent replacement; late-child failure retains parent segment identities and avoids fetch/evaluation.",
    "Compiler literal emission preserves unused and linker-retained private declarations; existing module hash and artifact v3 envelope remain the authenticity owner.",
    "Host verifies emitted bytes before execution and registry admission, injects registry into native/protected sessions and preserves it in checkpoint candidates.",
    "Preexisting nonnominal identity inputs and all preexisting ABI manifest contents remain unchanged; registry capability admission is exact JSON, including bool/int distinctions."
